Suggest ready-to-paste paths between two points; never edits the file

Usage: kashika route [OPTIONS] <FILE> [REST]...

Arguments:
  <FILE>     Input .kash file, or `-` for stdin
  [REST]...  `<from> <to>` points (e.g. `app1.bottom pg.left@0.25`), then an optional style: corner (default), arc or bezier. With `--line`, the points may be omitted

Options:
      --line <LINE>              Reroute this existing line, keeping its id and attributes
      --radius <RADIUS>          Corner radius for the `arc` style [default: 8]
      --max <MAX>                Number of candidates to print [default: 3]
      --format <FORMAT>          [default: text] [possible values: text, json]
      --allow-path               Allow file references outside the input file's directory
      --include <FILE>           Allow this one file outside the input file's directory (repeatable; relative to the current directory)
      --stdin-name <STDIN_NAME>  File name to report for stdin input
  -h, --help                     Print help
